# Prettier is scoped to *.json and src/components/** ONLY (see the "lint-staged"
# block in package.json). The rest of the tree is intentionally NOT prettier-managed
# and must keep its original hand-written style — listing it here stops an accidental
# `prettier --write .` (or on a specific file) from reformatting it:
#
#   src/js/**  — legacy code inherited from the robertabcd/PttChrome fork. A mass
#                reformat wipes git blame on the fragile render / BBS-protocol core
#                (term_view / term_buf / pttchrome / ansi_parser …) and risks silent
#                behaviour changes in code with thin (e2e-only) test coverage.
#   src/css/** — hand-maintained stylesheets.
#   dist/**    — build output.
#   tests/unit/fixtures/ptt_src_screens/** — written by tools/ptt-src-screens; the
#                scheduled workflow compares a fresh run to them with `git diff`, so a
#                reformat reads as an upstream screen change on every run.
#
# If src/js ever really needs unifying, do it as ONE isolated "prettier all of src/js"
# commit (no logic changes) so the churn is quarantined — never mixed into a feature diff.
src/js/
src/css/
dist/
tests/unit/fixtures/ptt_src_screens/
